{{also|Kalima|калима}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ar|كَلِمَة||word}}
{{root|en|ar|ك ل م}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|Islam}} the [[formal]] [[content]] of the [[shahada]] ([[declaration]] of [[faith]]): {{l|ar|لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا ٱللَّٰهُ مُحَمَّدٌ رَسُولُ ٱللَّٰهِ}} "There is no God but Allah, and Muhammad is the messenger of Allah."

====Usage notes====
The [[Quranist]] kalima may be as follows: {{m|ar||لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا ٱللَّٰهُ وَحْدَهُ لَا شَرِيكَ لَهُ|gloss=There is no deity but God, he hath no partners}}.

